/* =====================================================================
   point-of-view-core.js — the model for ACTIVITY #119 of the one-by-one
   rebuild: "Lumen's Lighthouse Windows" → THE WINDOW THAT SHOWS WHAT IT
   SEES (RL.1.6; all 11 locales).
   Design: docs/activities-rebuild/designs/119-point-of-view.md
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Three creatures look out of a lighthouse from a high, a middle and a
   low window. Choose a window and the harbor appears exactly as that
   creature sees it: from the top the boat is a tiny dot far below, from
   the middle it is straight across, from the bottom it is huge and close.
   · Level 1 "From which window?": the storyteller's words (tiny and far /
     straight across / huge and close) match only one window's view.
   · Level 2 "Who tells each part?": three lines of one story, each told
     by one creature; a line names a body part only its teller has (wings,
     a long thin tail, long ears, pincers…) or a view only its window
     gives. One creature may tell two parts.
   DATA is written by a build script that checks every line's view words
   and every part against the creatures' closed lists.
   Pure and DOM-free; UMD (window.LumenWindowsCore / require()).
   ===================================================================== */
